.el .ds Aq '
.TH rev-stealth-browser-launch 1  "rev-stealth-browser-launch " 
.SH NAME
rev\-stealth\-browser\-launch \- Launch a stealth browser, navigate to a URL, and emit JSON about the resulting page (UA / viewport / title / final URL). Useful as a smoke test that the launcher works on this host
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBrev\-stealth browser launch\fR [\fB\-\-profile\fR] [\fB\-\-stealth\fR] [\fB\-\-url\fR] [\fB\-\-headed\fR] [\fB\-\-chrome\fR] [\fB\-\-dwell\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Launch a chromiumoxide\-driven stealth browser with the chosen profile and stealth level, navigate to \-\-url, and dump page metadata (UA / viewport / title / final URL). Use for launcher smoke tests on a new host.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-profile\fR \fI<PROFILE>\fR [default: mobile\-ios]
Profile slug. One of: `desktop`, `mobile\-ios`, `mobile\-android`, `ipad`, `galaxy\-ultra`
.TP
\fB\-\-stealth\fR \fI<STEALTH>\fR [default: full]
Stealth level: `off`, `basic`, `full`
.TP
\fB\-\-url\fR \fI<URL>\fR [default: about:blank]
Navigate to this URL after launch. Default: `about:blank`
.TP
\fB\-\-headed\fR
Run with a visible chrome window instead of new\-headless mode
.TP
\fB\-\-chrome\fR \fI<CHROME>\fR
Override the chrome executable path. By default, chromiumoxide auto\-detects the system chrome
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBREV_STEALTH_CHROME\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-dwell\fR \fI<DWELL>\fR [default: 0]
Hold the page for this many seconds after navigation (lets a detector finish its work). Default 0 = exit as soon as `document.readyState` settles
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.SH EXTRA
EXAMPLES:
  $ rev\-stealth browser launch
  $ rev\-stealth browser launch \-\-profile desktop \-\-url https://example.com \-\-dwell 3
  $ rev\-stealth browser launch \-\-headed \-\-stealth full \-\-chrome /usr/bin/google\-chrome

EXIT CODES:
  0  Ok               Launch + navigation succeeded.
  1  UserError        Unknown \-\-profile / \-\-stealth slug.
  2  TransientError   Chrome launch/CDP transient failure.
  3  PermanentError   Chrome binary missing or stealth level unsupported.

ENV:
  REV_STEALTH_CHROME  Override the chrome executable path (else auto\-detect).
